FILE: app/src/fly-controls.ts
```ts
import type { FreeCamera, SceneContext } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { attachConfigurableFreeControl } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function attachFlyControls(
  camera: FreeCamera,
  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,
  scene: SceneContext
): () => void {
  return attachConfigurableFreeControl(camera, canvas, scene, {
    upKeys: ["Space", " "],
    downKeys: ["PageDown"],
    fastKeys: ["Shift", "ShiftLeft", "ShiftRight"],
    fastMultiplier: 3,
  });
}
```

I created `src/fly-controls.ts` to attach the library’s configurable free-camera controls with Space/PageDown for vertical movement and Shift as a 3× speed key, returning the library’s detach function so no extra listeners or per-frame work remain. I was not fully sure whether the library matches `event.key` or `event.code`, so I included both common spellings for Space and Shift.
